[36m==>[0m Preflight checks (user mode)
  [31m✗[0m AppArmor restricts unprivileged user namespaces (Ubuntu 23.10+) — a user install can't lift this
  [33m![0m   fix (root): echo 'kernel.apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns=0' | sudo tee /etc/sysctl.d/99-xbin.conf && sudo sysctl --system
  [32m✓[0m cgroup v2 present (per-component accounting)
  [32m✓[0m /dev/fuse present (fuse-overlayfs; apt in terminals works)
  [32m✓[0m /dev/net/tun present (egress relay / terminal internet scope)
  [32m✓[0m /dev/kvm present (VM sandboxes on KVM, for terminals and backends)
  [33m![0m /dev/kvm is not usable by mira — VM sandboxes would run emulated (slower); for KVM run once as root: sudo usermod -aG kvm mira, then log in again (or: sudo systemctl restart user@1000)
  [32m✓[0m systemd user manager reachable (systemctl --user)
  [31m✗[0m missing tools (a user install can't add packages): newuidmap newgidmap
  [33m![0m   run once as root:  sudo apt-get install -y uidmap
  [32m✓[0m subuid: range present for mira
  [32m✓[0m subgid: range present for mira
  [33m![0m fs.inotify.max_user_watches=30241 is low — recommended (root): echo 'fs.inotify.max_user_watches=524288' | sudo tee /etc/sysctl.d/99-xbin.conf && sudo sysctl --system
  [33m![0m container tiles (cap:containers) will need user_allow_other in /etc/fuse.conf — run once as root: echo user_allow_other | sudo tee -a /etc/fuse.conf
  [33m![0m user-mode preflight has blockers (✗ above) — fix them, or pick the system install (it can)

[36m==>[0m [1mThis will (system mode):[0m
   1. install packages via apt: uidmap fuse3 git ca-certificates curl tar (missing: newuidmap newgidmap)
   2. download + verify the prebuilt bundle for amd64 (this release's manifest) — no podman/Go, no build
   3. create system user xbin (home /opt/xbin)
   4. delegate subuid/subgid 100000+65536 to xbin (/etc/subuid, /etc/subgid)
   5. load + persist the KVM module and add xbin to the kvm group (VM sandboxes)
   6. persist fuse+tun autoload + raise inotify watches + lift the AppArmor userns restriction (/etc/modules-load.d, /etc/sysctl.d)
   7. verify a user namespace comes up for xbin
   8. install binaries → /opt/xbin/bin, base rootfs → /opt/xbin/rootfs (copies a few GB), SDK → /opt/xbin/sdk; workspace dir /opt/xbin/workspace; link bx → /usr/local/bin/bx
   9. turn VM sandboxes on in /opt/xbin/workspace/.xbin/vm/policy.json (never configured): terminals + backends + tile sandboxes with a usable KVM, terminals only where they'd run emulated; nothing without the VM pieces
  10. choose vault unseal mode (auto → passphrase stored in /etc/xbin/xbin.env mode 600, or manual unseal each boot)
  11. write systemd unit /etc/systemd/system/xbin.service + daemon-reload
  12. exclude xbin.service from needrestart auto-restart (/etc/needrestart/conf.d/xbin.conf)
  13. enable + start the unit, wait for /healthz on 127.0.0.1:8642
  then: print the one-time login URL (journalctl -u xbin)
      (probes ran read-only without root; after sudo, preflight and this plan are re-verified, re-printed, and confirmed before anything changes)

